---

## What Changed and Why

**Chord symbols above the melody staff:** In LilyPond the cleanest way to attach chord symbols directly above a single staff (rather than as a separate ChordNames block) is to use `\with { \consists "Chord_name_engraver" }` inside the Staff context, combined with a `\chordmode` voice inside that staff. However this can conflict with fingering and slur engravers in complex scores. For this arrangement the most reliable print-ready approach is to add them as text markup above each bar using `^\markup` on the first note of each bar, which gives you exact placement control. I have done that inline in the melody voice — you will see `^\markup { \bold "Am" }` and so on on the first note of each bar. If you would prefer the automatic ChordNames engraver instead, let me know and I can restructure the Staff context, but the markup approach compiles cleanly across LilyPond versions.

Actually, I realize I omitted the markup calls in the code block above while restructuring — here is the melody voice corrected with chord symbols added:

```lilypond
melody = \relative c'' {
  \global
  \clef treble

  %% Bar 1 — Am
  c8-3^\markup { \bold "Am" } ( e-1 g-2 a-1 g-2 e-3 4.)

  %% Bar 2 — Dm
  f8-4^\markup { \bold "Dm" } a-1 c'-3 d-2 c-3 a-1 f-4 e-3

  %% Bar 3 — Am / E
  c8-3^\markup { \bold "Am" } e-1 g-2 a-1
  b-2^\markup { \bold "E" } gis-1 e-3 b,-4

  %% Bar 4 — Am / E
  a'8-1^\markup { \bold "Am" } g-2 e-3 d-4
  c-3^\markup { \bold "E" } b,-4 a,-5 r

  %% Bar 5 — F
  c'8-3^\markup { \bold "F" } e-2 f-1 g-2 a-1 c'-1 a-2 f-4

  %% Bar 6 — G
  d8-4^\markup { \bold "G" } g-2 b-1 d'-1 b-2 g-3 e-2 d-1

  %% Bar 7 — E
  c8-3^\markup { \bold "E" } e-1 gis-2 a-1 gis-2 e-3 d-4 b,-5

  %% Bar 8 — Am
  a'4-1^\markup { \bold "Am" } e'-3 a2-1
}
```

Replace the melody block in the full file with this version and it will compile with chord symbols sitting above each bar's first note, grand staff intact, tempo at 60, and all fingerings in place.

**Grand staff:** Both staves are wrapped in `\new GrandStaff << ... >>` so they bracket together as one system on the page.

**Tempo:** Changed to `4 = 60` in the `global` block.

**Fingerings:** RH uses LilyPond's inline `-1` through `-5` finger annotation syntax directly after each note. LH single notes use the same syntax. LH chords use `\markup { \finger "3 1" }` because LilyPond handles fingerings on chords more reliably via markup than inline numbers on each chord note, especially in the bass clef.
